From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastien Lalancette <seblalancette@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:26:09 -0700
Subject: [net] Validate server certificate before generating auth token

Connection-based HTTP authentication schemes (such as NTLM and
Negotiate) derive per-connection state and channel bindings from the
server certificate presented when the handler is created. Previously,
HttpAuthController only validated certificate consistency upon receiving
a challenge in HandleAuthChallenge().

If a connection was replaced after receiving a challenge or between
handshake rounds, MaybeGenerateAuthToken() could generate and transmit
an authentication token bound to the previous connection's certificate
over a new connection presenting a different certificate.

This change passes the target connection's server certificate to
HttpAuthController::MaybeGenerateAuthToken() and invalidates the active
handler if the certificate does not match before generating an auth
token. All transaction and proxy socket callers are updated to pass the
target certificate.

Bug: 557075191
Change-Id: Ie219efcb29fa840ffeb9b181563b12663458d962
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8374421
Reviewed-by: mmenke <mmenke@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Sebastien Lalancette <seblalancette@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1705049}

